===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*peh₂w-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|pullulātus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|pullulō||sprout forth}}, from {{m|la|pullulus||a young animal, a sprout}}, diminutive of {{m|la|pullus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpʌl.jʊ.leɪt/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-pullulate.ogg|a=US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[multiply]] [[rapid]]ly.
# To [[germinate]].
# To [[teem]]; to be filled (''with'').
#* {{RQ:Waugh Brideshead Revisited|chapter=1|page=22|passage=I must say the whole of Oxford has become ''most'' peculiar suddenly. Last night it was '''pullulating''' with women.}}

